WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:01.445
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.445 --> 00:00:04.609
today's message is compromise.

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:06.388
Over to you Ryan Gosling.

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:08.297
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.297 --> 00:00:11.011
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.807
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.807 --> 00:00:18.058
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:19.975
- I think compromise...

00:00:22.282 --> 00:00:23.361
is integral

00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:27.799
to the creative process, and
it's more about finding a way

00:00:27.799 --> 00:00:32.591
to make those compromises

00:00:32.591 --> 00:00:36.758
into opportunities

00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:42.144
and not see them as obstacles.

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:45.027
Otherwise you can get really stuck.

00:00:45.027 --> 00:00:48.659
I think that's the only
way to keep moving forward

00:00:48.659 --> 00:00:50.290
and being creative.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.042
- So this is an interesting
message for this channel

00:00:52.042 --> 00:00:55.636
because so often people are
coming in, saying go for it,

00:00:55.636 --> 00:00:58.555
never give up, go, push
harder and here's a message

00:00:58.555 --> 00:00:59.521
saying compromise.

00:00:59.521 --> 00:01:01.868
And I think it's actually when you look

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.279
at the most successful entrepreneurs

00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:06.870
and the most successful
leaders, it's both.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.676
It's the genius of the and.

00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:12.426
You will see that the
most successful leaders

00:01:13.578 --> 00:01:18.210
are insanely stubborn for the why

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.156
but insanely flexible about the how

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:24.598
and this is where a lot of
entrepreneurs will fall short

00:01:24.598 --> 00:01:27.623
because you're so obsessed
about doing this thing

00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:31.086
in a particular way
that it may not work out

00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:32.725
and chances are it won't.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.479
Chances are that product
that you want to put out,

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:36.047
people may not like the design,

00:01:36.047 --> 00:01:37.658
they may not like the functionality,

00:01:37.658 --> 00:01:40.718
it may not work exactly
as you thought it would

00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:42.945
and you need to tweak it,
you need to change it,

00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:45.153
you need to listen,
you need to compromise.

00:01:45.153 --> 00:01:48.193
But what you won't
compromise is the big vision.

00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:51.680
What you won't compromise
on, is your one word,

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.258
your value right, like
this is what you stand for

00:01:54.258 --> 00:01:56.620
and that's the line in the sand

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.503
and you're not going to go over it.

00:01:58.503 --> 00:02:02.105
Where I think most people are
stubborn about small things,

00:02:02.105 --> 00:02:04.806
I think most people are
stubborn about the wrong things.

00:02:04.806 --> 00:02:06.302
I think most people are so stubborn

00:02:06.302 --> 00:02:07.988
that they hold themselves back

00:02:07.988 --> 00:02:09.448
because they're not willing to compromise

00:02:09.448 --> 00:02:11.120
to get to the big goal.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.612
What you need to have, is the ego

00:02:15.612 --> 00:02:19.340
to believe that you can do
the big thing, the confidence

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.427
and the boldness to go
and chase that big dream

00:02:22.427 --> 00:02:26.453
and then at the same time,
the humbleness for the cause.

00:02:26.453 --> 00:02:29.906
You can do this big
thing, you're confident

00:02:29.906 --> 00:02:32.952
you have the ego to do
it but the humbleness

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.956
to do anything needed to go out and do it.

00:02:35.956 --> 00:02:38.368
Maybe that means you
have to sweep the floors.

00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:39.679
Anything!

00:02:39.679 --> 00:02:42.512
The great leaders will do anything

00:02:43.504 --> 00:02:47.133
to move their cause
forward, as long as it falls

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.135
within the lines of who they are

00:02:50.135 --> 00:02:51.727
but nothing is beneath them.

00:02:51.727 --> 00:02:53.899
They'll get on the assembly
line and start making products

00:02:53.899 --> 00:02:55.994
if they need to, they'll
make the phone calls

00:02:55.994 --> 00:02:57.807
if they need to, they'll sweep the floors

00:02:57.807 --> 00:02:59.593
if they need to.

00:02:59.593 --> 00:03:03.471
And so, if you're being stubborn
about something right now

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:04.992
I would really challenge you to think,

00:03:04.992 --> 00:03:08.134
"Does this actually matter?"

00:03:08.134 --> 00:03:11.587
Because the most important
thing is advancing the cause.

00:03:11.587 --> 00:03:16.485
Stubbornness around the
why, the mission, the cause

00:03:16.485 --> 00:03:20.652
and flexibility around the
execution and how to do it.

00:03:21.508 --> 00:03:22.917
That's my thoughts.

00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:24.287
What do you think?

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:28.183
I want to know, in your
life, in your business,

00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:30.998
what is non-negotiable,
what are you not willing

00:03:30.998 --> 00:03:35.815
to compromise on, I'm curious.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.266
Leave in the comments below,
I want to see your answers.

00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:40.028
I also want to give a
big shout out to Jeff.

00:03:40.028 --> 00:03:42.327
Jeff, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:03:42.327 --> 00:03:44.788
Your One Word, it really
really really means a lot

00:03:44.788 --> 00:03:46.889
to me man, appreciate the support.

00:03:46.889 --> 00:03:49.072
Thank you guys for
watching, I believe in you,

00:03:49.072 --> 00:03:51.006
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:03:51.006 --> 00:03:53.219
and whatever your one word is.

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:55.427
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:03:55.427 --> 00:03:58.095
for another shot of Espresso.

00:03:58.095 --> 00:04:00.568
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:00.568 --> 00:04:04.460
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:05.384
What's up Believe Nation.

00:04:05.384 --> 00:04:07.677
To add some more perspective on this idea

00:04:07.677 --> 00:04:10.247
of compromising, I'm going to
put a couple more bonus clips

00:04:10.247 --> 00:04:11.932
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:04:11.932 --> 00:04:15.344
- I have no education, I
had no high school diploma,

00:04:15.344 --> 00:04:18.672
I didn't even have a GED
because I quit high school

00:04:18.672 --> 00:04:20.755
halfway through grade 10.

00:04:21.741 --> 00:04:24.121
I didn't have a lot of
options, I would be dishwasher,

00:04:24.121 --> 00:04:27.621
a waiter, a custodial worker of some sort.

00:04:28.802 --> 00:04:32.894
So I decided I might as well
go and do something creative,

00:04:32.894 --> 00:04:35.948
I decided to go to the
comedy store, Laugh Factory

00:04:35.948 --> 00:04:40.115
and The Improv, all of
those clubs every night

00:04:41.602 --> 00:04:45.769
and make my 25 bucks a pop, a set.

00:04:46.764 --> 00:04:51.001
It was my version of being a
waiter, it was a compromise

00:04:51.001 --> 00:04:52.821
I decided to make.

00:04:52.821 --> 00:04:55.506
Out of that came "In Living Color"

00:04:55.506 --> 00:04:59.713
and out of that came touring, auditoriums,

00:04:59.713 --> 00:05:01.000
5,000 seaters.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.440
It was a really creative time.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.306
I was able to prove,
that I didn't have to be

00:05:05.306 --> 00:05:08.796
an impressionist, that I
had a personality of my own

00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:12.128
and however abrasive it
might be from time to time.

00:05:12.128 --> 00:05:14.924
Long story short, all of it
came from that compromise,

00:05:14.924 --> 00:05:19.259
from that deciding to do
what I didn't want to do.

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:22.423
The things you can't
do or the things you're

00:05:22.423 --> 00:05:25.008
not allowed to do, like if
the executives come and say

00:05:25.008 --> 00:05:28.673
you can't do that, whatever
it is, it's too expesnive,

00:05:28.673 --> 00:05:31.078
you get angry, you get
out of your mind about it

00:05:31.078 --> 00:05:33.286
because you've been
clinging to this concept

00:05:33.286 --> 00:05:36.188
and this image that you have
of how it should be done,

00:05:36.188 --> 00:05:41.003
and invariably, most times,

00:05:41.003 --> 00:05:43.313
after that storm has passed

00:05:43.313 --> 00:05:45.288
and you actually sit down and go okay,

00:05:45.288 --> 00:05:47.706
we can't do it that way, how can we do it,

00:05:47.706 --> 00:05:50.511
you end up with something even better

00:05:50.511 --> 00:05:53.488
than what was there before and you go,

00:05:53.488 --> 00:05:56.180
that's the universe and
that's how it works.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.669
It's like relationships,
it's like everything.

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.192
The thing that is taken away,
that you're clinging to,

00:06:02.192 --> 00:06:04.975
that you're trying to fix and
you're trying to secure it,

00:06:04.975 --> 00:06:06.734
make sure it doesn't go away.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:08.734
You think your life will be destroyed,

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:11.925
everything will be ruined and
it's just the universe going,

00:06:11.925 --> 00:06:14.243
no, I have something better for you.

00:06:14.243 --> 00:06:18.119
Just have faith, sometimes
compromise is actually the way

00:06:18.119 --> 00:06:19.945
to get to what you want

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:24.514
- I have a certain gene
in my body that allows me

00:06:24.514 --> 00:06:29.443
to understand what someone else is saying

00:06:29.443 --> 00:06:32.291
when they say we want to
sell a lot of these things.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:35.835
Like I don't see selling
a bunch of something,

00:06:35.835 --> 00:06:40.009
as the opposite of it being
interesting, or important,

00:06:40.009 --> 00:06:41.176
or meaningful.

00:06:44.462 --> 00:06:46.626
I've always seen it from both sides

00:06:46.626 --> 00:06:50.793
and it's a really interesting
place that I'm in right now.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:54.728
You do have to balance.

00:06:56.271 --> 00:07:01.088
If you saw my iTunes playlist,
I could have a conversation

00:07:01.088 --> 00:07:04.717
with anybody at Stereogum or Pitchfork

00:07:04.717 --> 00:07:09.002
but what I do with Columbia
Records as the artiste

00:07:09.002 --> 00:07:11.163
that I am with the records that I make

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:15.152
under the contract that
I have, I'm taking all

00:07:15.152 --> 00:07:17.702
of my influences and I'm
trying to convert them

00:07:17.702 --> 00:07:20.862
into pop music, that's my job right now.

00:07:20.862 --> 00:07:22.537
It's not the only thing I can do,

00:07:22.537 --> 00:07:24.144
and it's not the only thing I will do,

00:07:24.144 --> 00:07:28.311
but as long as I'm still
trying to make pop songs,

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.857
I want to play by pop rules.

00:07:32.863 --> 00:07:35.806
I want to listen to top 20 and
figure out what's going on,

00:07:35.806 --> 00:07:36.941
I don't want to fall behind.

00:07:36.941 --> 00:07:40.950
I'm trying to take all the
elements of music that I love,

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.936
that I'm well versed in and convert them

00:07:43.936 --> 00:07:47.235
into music that a lot
of people can get into.

00:07:47.235 --> 00:07:49.308
I don't know why I do that.

00:07:49.308 --> 00:07:50.656
A lot of people can't, a lot of people

00:07:50.656 --> 00:07:52.681
find the compromise maddening.

00:07:52.681 --> 00:07:54.462
I see it as another challenge

00:07:54.462 --> 00:07:56.572
and I see it as another talent,

00:07:56.572 --> 00:07:59.760
like the ultimate talent of restraint.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.007
- All filmmaking is
intelligent compromise,

00:08:03.007 --> 00:08:05.735
that's the whole process we go through.

00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.978
I mean, Con will be
able to vouch for this,

00:08:07.978 --> 00:08:09.975
no matter what your budget,
you never have enough time

00:08:09.975 --> 00:08:12.617
you never have enough money.

00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:15.197
It's weird when you're doing a huge film,

00:08:15.197 --> 00:08:16.373
you're in the same position you were,

00:08:16.373 --> 00:08:18.421
when you were doing a tiny film.

00:08:18.421 --> 00:08:19.616
And there's a good reason for that,

00:08:19.616 --> 00:08:22.078
you're always trying to
get as much on screen

00:08:22.078 --> 00:08:23.397
as you possibly can.

00:08:23.397 --> 00:08:25.747
And so whatever the box
that's built for you

00:08:25.747 --> 00:08:28.274
by the economics of the
project you're always trying

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.297
to push up against those walls

00:08:30.297 --> 00:08:31.629
and so you need help from your team

00:08:31.629 --> 00:08:33.542
in terms of how arrange things

00:08:33.542 --> 00:08:35.902
and how you make that work.

00:08:35.902 --> 00:08:39.534
- Waking up every
morning and compromising.

00:08:39.534 --> 00:08:41.953
You have this idea, this
ideal of what you want

00:08:41.953 --> 00:08:46.682
to do that day and you then, you know,

00:08:46.682 --> 00:08:48.457
it just gets stripped
away and stripped away

00:08:48.457 --> 00:08:49.724
and stripped away and stripped away,

00:08:49.724 --> 00:08:53.461
except for those magnificent moments

00:08:53.461 --> 00:08:57.694
when they cast does something
that you couldn't imagine

00:08:57.694 --> 00:09:00.870
and you go wow, that is really awesome.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.377
And then you immediately get a feeling

00:09:03.377 --> 00:09:06.512
of dread, because you're expecting then

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:09.160
as soon as you say cut,
that someone will say

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.842
yeah, we missed the focus,

00:09:11.842 --> 00:09:14.151
there was a boom in the shot,

00:09:14.151 --> 00:09:17.413
there was an extra in the
background, who tripped and fell,

00:09:17.413 --> 00:09:20.407
whatever the thing is
that ruined the moment,

00:09:20.407 --> 00:09:21.849
that you may not get back again.

